# Popeye audio output stage -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Couriersud's netlist of Popeye's audio: the three AY-3-8910 channels through R52-R60 and
# C4-C6 to a mixing node (R51, R57, R60, R61, C40) and C7, then the impedance changer Q8/Q9
# (R62-R67), which MAME's file calls 'solely an impedance changer', to the TV's audio on edge
# pin W. The AY's outputs are ports.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/nintendo/nl_popeye.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(popeye). Licence BSD-3-Clause by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Couriersud (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/nintendo/nl_popeye.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Corrected from the TPP2-CPU schematic, sheet 2 of 3 (manual p. 35):
#   R65: the sheet's value is 5.1K, MAME's 2100 -- the schematic prints 5.1K, and the parts list has R65 among its 5.1K resistors
# line 49: AY_A is not a part -- the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on channel A, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_1)
# line 50: AY_B is not a part -- the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on channel B, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_2)
# line 51: AY_C is not a part -- the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on channel C, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_3)
# line 65: TV_AUDIO is not a part -- the load on the output, which MAME's file says is 'actually located in TV' (ROUT); R67 goes to edge pin W, 'TV AUDIO'
#
# Compared with the TPP2-CPU schematic, sheet 2 of 3 (manual doc a4dc252b9a5e p. 35, clearly
# legible), and the typeset parts list (p. 27), on 2026-10-20: all 14 nets agree, and every
# value but one -- R65 is 5.1K on both the sheet and the parts list, where MAME has 2.1K,
# corrected above. Q8 is a 2SC1815 and Q9 a 2SA1015 as MAME has them. One designator is in
# doubt: the schematic letters the mixer's 20K 'R51', as MAME does, but also prints an R51
# on sheet 3, a 100 ohm in the sync buffer, and the parts list has R51 at 100 ohms and R54 as
# its only 20K -- so on the board this is most likely R54. Where R52's lead crosses channel
# B the drawing is broken; only this file's reading (R52 from the AY's pin 4 to ground)
# works. D2 (1S1595), a clamp on the AY's supply, is on the sheet and not in MAME.


value R51 20000
value R52 2000
value R53 2000
value R55 2000
value R56 2000
value R57 30000
value R58 2000
value R59 2000
value R60 30000
value R61 120000
value R62 510000
value R63 100
value R64 510000
value R65 5.1K
value R66 330
value R67 51
value C4 0.047e-6
value C5 330e-12
value C6 330e-12
value C7 3.3e-6
value C40 680e-12
value Q8 2SC1815
value Q9 2SA1015

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supplies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net GND: C4.2 C40.2 C5.2 C6.2 Q9.C R52.2 R55.2 R58.2 R61.2 R64.2 R65.2
net +5V: Q8.C R62.1 R66.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# It is solely an impedance changer and could be left away
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire C7.2 R62.2 R63.1 R64.1
wire Q8.B R63.2
wire Q8.E Q9.B R65.1
wire Q9.E R66.2 R67.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AY 8910 internal resistors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port AY_A: R52.1 R53.1  # in MAME: AY_A, not part: the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on channel A, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_1)
port AY_B: R55.1 R56.1  # in MAME: AY_B, not part: the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on channel B, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_2)
port AY_C: R58.1 R59.1  # in MAME: AY_C, not part: the AY-3-8910's own output resistance on channel C, which MAME draws as a 1K resistor from +5V (R_AY1_3)
wire C4.1 R51.1 R53.2
wire C5.1 R56.2 R57.1
wire C6.1 R59.2 R60.1
wire C40.1 C7.1 R51.2 R57.2 R60.2 R61.1
port TV_AUDIO: R67.2  # in MAME: TV_AUDIO, not part: the load on the output, which MAME's file says is 'actually located in TV' (ROUT); R67 goes to edge pin W, 'TV AUDIO'

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins with nothing attached
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
